{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultByteBound","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory"],"anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Type Properties"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"code":["let store = try SegmentStore(events: [SignedUp.self, CheckedOut.self])","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write-through."}]},{"text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, with one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write()"},{"text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"power loss too (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"text":", as the app moves to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"background or terminates.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What is kept."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Only events of the types in ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which conform to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are delivered in this run like any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other, are never written, and produce no drop report, but are lost if the app ends first.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record’s context is not kept: a recovered record is in the top-level ","type":"text"},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as its span ended with the earlier run.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Deleting.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. There is no compaction: a segment kept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for one undelivered record keeps its delivered ones too."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bound."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The log never holds more than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"type":"text","text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered yields a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":". A record too large for an empty log"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is kept in memory only."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"comes back with "},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Other versions.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound. A segment in an earlier version, which this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one can’t read, is deleted and reported as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changed event types."}]},{"text":" Each record’s event is a map of its properties by name, so a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before its type changed still reads: a property removed since is skipped and an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional one added since is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":". One that can’t, after a required property was added or a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property’s type changed, is dropped and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store share its log."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore"},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SegmentStore.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L54"},"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","title":"SegmentStore","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV"},"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/BinaryCodable":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryCodable","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BinaryCodable","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A value with a compact binary form, CBOR (RFC 8949), that a store keeps on disk."}],"title":"BinaryCodable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/binarycodable","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/pendingRecordCount":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"pendingRecordCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"}],"title":"pendingRecordCount","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/pendingrecordcount","abstract":[{"text":"How many records the log keeps that are not yet delivered.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount","role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/synchronize()":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"synchronize()","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/synchronize()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Flushes every segment written since the last flush to storage ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","tex